title: APC Netbotz Devices: Temperature Sensor
agents: snmp
catalog: hw/power/apc
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors the temperature sensors of APC Netbotz devices
 which support the NETBOTZV2 MIB, e.g. Netbotz 450 series, or the
 NETBOTZ50 MIB, e.g. Netbotz 50.

 It also monitors the wireless temperature sensors (NBWS100T, NBWS100H)
 of the Netbotz Rack Monitor series, e.g. Netbotz 250. Those devices
 report their wireless sensors via the wirelessSensorStatusTable of the
 PowerNet MIB instead of one of the Netbotz MIBs.

 You can configure lower and upper levels for {CRIT} and {WARN}
 (default: {WARN}: 25, 30 {CRIT}: 20, 35)

 The service goes {WARN} or {CRIT} if the temperature is higher
 than given upper levels or lower than the given lower levels.
 Otherwise it returns {OK}.

 This check uses the NETBOTZV2-MIB, the NETBOTZ50-MIB and the PowerNet-MIB.

item:
 The temperature sensor identifier. For wireless sensors this is the sensor
 name configured on the device, or {Wireless sensor <index>} if the sensor
 has no name.

discovery:
 One service is created for each temperature sensor.
